CAPSTONE PROJECT
Project Planning


# Objective

The objective of this project is to perform an authorized penetration test against the intentionally vulnerable Metasploitable 2 virtual machine using Kali Linux.
The project will be performed in an isolated virtual laboratory consisting of two virtual machines:

| System   | Operating System | Role                            | IP Address     |
| -------- | ---------------- | ------------------------------- | -------------- |
| Attacker | Kali Linux       | Penetration-testing             | 10.0.2.15/24   |
| Target   | Metasploitable 2 | Intentionally vulnerable target | 192.168.56.103 |

#Scope

The scope of the assessment includes:

* Metasploitable 2 virtual machine
* Web applications hosted on the target
* Network services exposed by the target
* Evidence and screenshot collection
* Risk assessment
* Mitigation recommendations
* Controlled incident-response simulation

#Tools 

| Tool                 | Purpose                                          |
| -------------------- | ------------------------------------------------ |
| Kali Linux           | Main penetration-testing platform                |
| Metasploitable 2     | Intentionally vulnerable target                  |
| Nmap                 | Network discovery                                |
| Burp Suite           | Web application analysis and testing             |
| Metasploit Framework | Controlled vulnerability validation/exploitation |
| Web Browser          | Accessing and testing web applications           |
| Netcat               | Network/service verification where required      |
| Terminal             | Command execution and evidence collection        |
| Screenshot utility   | Documentation of testing evidence                |
| VirtualBox/VMware    | Virtual laboratory environment                   |

